      "created_at": "2026-01-22T16:44:58.364Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi,</p>\n<p>I’ve searched on existing posts but I didn’t find the solution.</p>\n<p>I’ve a structure like this:</p>\n<p>Parent DocType: Brand</p>\n<p>Field 1: Brand name (data field)</p>\n<p>Field 2: Model (a Table field)</p>\n<p>Child DocType: Model (set as Child Table)</p>\n<p>Field 1: Model name (data field)</p>\n<p>So I have a simple structure where I can add a Brand and inside it add multiple Models see image:</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/1/0/10f36bd8ad6e7e99c02814a986917d418dc3a2af.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/10f36bd8ad6e7e99c02814a986917d418dc3a2af\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/1/0/10f36bd8ad6e7e99c02814a986917d418dc3a2af_2_690x205.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"2pXamJij7kGVxsExJvM3KyraAcn\" width=\"690\" height=\"205\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/1/0/10f36bd8ad6e7e99c02814a986917d418dc3a2af_2_690x205.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/1/0/10f36bd8ad6e7e99c02814a986917d418dc3a2af_2_1035x307.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/1/0/10f36bd8ad6e7e99c02814a986917d418dc3a2af.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"FBFCFB\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1099×327 16.3 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>I have created a DocType where I have 2 fields:</p>\n<p>Field 1: Brand (link field)</p>\n<p>Field 2: Model (link field)</p>\n<p>What I need is to filter Model items by Brand selected field (if I select Brand 1, I want that Model field shows only Models from Brand 1)</p>\n<p>I think that the script in my form would be something similar:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">brand(frm) {\n    frm.set_query(\"model\", (doc) =&gt; {\n        return {\n            filters: {\n                \"brand_field\": doc.brand\n            }\n        }\n    });\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Instead of “<strong>brand_field</strong>” I need to refer to the parent brand field of the model doctype, but model doctype doesn’t have a brand field, because it is a child table. How can I filter the child doctype based on the brand selected field?</p>\n<p>I’ve tried using “parentfield” (<a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/framework/user/en/basics/doctypes/child-doctype\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Child / Table DocType</a>) but it doesn’t work.</p>\n<p>Thanks</p>",
